-- Q2491: Agency and Regulation [medium/L1]
-- Issues: #3
UPDATE questions SET
  explanation = $EXPL$Correct (D): Under the Restatement (Third) of Agency, Section 8.14, a principal owes the agent a duty to compensate as agreed and reimburse authorized expenses reasonably incurred while performing agency duties. Abbott traveled to client sites as instructed and submitted documented receipts, entitling him to reimbursement of the $3,200.
Wrong (A): No written employment contract is required before an agency relationship begins; agency can be created orally or by conduct.
Wrong (B): The principal has no duty to ensure the agent''s physical safety at all times, though workplace safety obligations may exist under other laws.
Wrong (C): There is no duty to disclose the principal''s complete financial records to the agent upon request.$EXPL$
