-- Q2500: Agency and Regulation [hard/L1]
-- Issues: #3
UPDATE questions SET
  explanation = $EXPL$Correct (B): Under the Restatement (Third) of Agency, Section 3.12, an agency coupled with an interest exists when the agent holds a security interest in the subject matter. Because the bank''s authority to sell the warehouse secures its $500,000 loan, the principal cannot unilaterally revoke this authority.
Wrong (A): An agency coupled with an interest cannot be freely revoked because the agent''s property interest in the subject matter must be protected.
Wrong (C): Unlike an ordinary agency, an agency coupled with an interest does not terminate upon the death or incapacity of the principal.
Wrong (D): An agency coupled with an interest is created by agreement between the parties, not by court order or judicial determination.$EXPL$
