-- Q2502: Agency and Regulation [medium/L2]
-- Issues: #3
UPDATE questions SET
  explanation = $EXPL$Correct (A): Under the Restatement (Third) of Agency, Section 8.11, an agent must use reasonable effort to provide the principal with facts that the agent knows or should know are material to the principal''s interests. A third party''s willingness to pay more than the asking price is clearly material and must be promptly communicated.
Wrong (B): Keeping this information confidential to negotiate a better commission would violate the agent''s fiduciary duty and constitute self-dealing.
Wrong (C): Selling at the asking price without informing the principal of the higher offer breaches the duty of notification by withholding material information.
Wrong (D): The duty of notification runs to the principal, not to a regulatory authority. There is no obligation to report pricing information to regulators.$EXPL$
