UPDATE questions SET
  explanation = $EXPL$Correct (C): Under IRC Sec. 1401, the self-employment tax rate is 15.3%, consisting of 12.4% for Social Security (OASDI) and 2.9% for Medicare (HI). This rate is applied to 92.35% of net self-employment earnings as specified in IRC Sec. 1402(a).
Wrong (A): 7.65% represents only the employee''s share of FICA. Self-employed individuals must pay both the employee and employer portions, totaling 15.3%.
Wrong (B): 12.4% is only the Social Security component. The full SE tax rate also includes the 2.9% Medicare component.
