  explanation = $EXPL$Correct (D): Under RULLCA Section 304, LLC members receive limited liability protection while retaining the right to actively participate in management. This is the key structural advantage over a general partnership, where management participation exposes partners to unlimited liability.
Wrong (A): This is incorrect—LLC members can participate in management without jeopardizing their liability protection, unlike limited partners under RULPA.
Wrong (B): An LLC may have a single member under most state statutes. There is no requirement for at least two members.
Wrong (C): LLCs are not always taxed as corporations. They may elect partnership taxation or disregarded-entity status under Treasury Regulation Section 301.7701-3.$EXPL$
