-- Q2514: Business Structures [medium/L2]
-- Issues: #3
UPDATE questions SET
  explanation = $EXPL$Correct (D): Under RULLCA Section 503, a creditor of an individual LLC member is limited to obtaining a charging order against the member''s transferable interest. The order entitles the creditor to receive distributions that would otherwise go to the debtor-member.
Wrong (A): A creditor with a personal judgment against a member cannot directly collect from LLC assets. The LLC is a separate legal entity from its members.
Wrong (B): The creditor cannot seize and sell the member''s LLC interest. The charging order is the exclusive remedy, preserving the other members'' rights.
Wrong (C): A personal judgment against one member does not give the creditor grounds to force dissolution of the entire LLC.$EXPL$
