-- Q2522: Business Structures [easy/L1]
-- Issues: #3
UPDATE questions SET
  explanation = $EXPL$Correct (B): Under RMBCA Section 2.02, articles of incorporation are filed with the state to legally create the corporation. Under RMBCA Section 2.06, bylaws are internal governance documents adopted by the board detailing meeting procedures, officer roles, and voting requirements.
Wrong (A): This reverses the distinction. Articles are the public filing; bylaws are the internal document—not the other way around.
Wrong (C): Only articles of incorporation must be filed with the state. Bylaws are adopted internally by the board and need not be filed.
Wrong (D): Under RMBCA, both the board and shareholders may adopt or amend bylaws. Articles of incorporation also require shareholder approval for amendments (Section 10.03).$EXPL$
WHERE id = 2522;

-- Q2523: Business Structures [medium/L2]
-- Issues: #3
UPDATE questions SET
  explanation = $EXPL$Correct (B): Sara''s initial tax basis is her $80,000 cash contribution plus her 40% share of the $200,000 nonrecourse liability ($80,000), totaling $160,000. Under IRC Sec. 752, a partner''s share of partnership liabilities increases their basis, and nonrecourse liabilities are generally allocated by profit-sharing ratios.
Wrong (A): $80,000 reflects only Sara''s cash contribution and ignores her allocable share of the nonrecourse debt.
Wrong (C): $120,000 would imply a 20% share of the debt rather than Sara''s actual 40% profit-sharing percentage.
Wrong (D): $280,000 would require allocating the entire $200,000 debt to Sara, not just her 40% share.$EXPL$
