-- Q2528: Business Structures [easy/L2]
-- Issues: #3
UPDATE questions SET
  explanation = $EXPL$Correct (C): Under IRC Sec. 702(a), each partner must include in gross income their distributive share of partnership items regardless of whether any distribution is actually made. Dave''s 50% share of $120,000 equals $60,000, reportable on his individual return.
Wrong (A): Partnership income is taxed to partners in the year earned, not deferred until withdrawn. Partnerships are pass-through entities under IRC Sec. 701.
Wrong (B): Dave''s reportable income is not limited to his capital contribution. His distributive share is based on the profit-sharing ratio, not the amount invested.
Wrong (D): Dave reports only his 50% distributive share, not the full $120,000. The other half is allocated to Ellen under the equal profit-sharing agreement.$EXPL$
