-- Q2529: Business Structures [hard/L2]
-- Issues: #3
UPDATE questions SET
  explanation = $EXPL$Correct (D): Under IRC Sec. 752, recourse liabilities are allocated to the partner who bears the economic risk of loss. Because Member A personally guaranteed the $100,000 debt, A bears the entire economic risk and the full liability is allocated to A''s basis.
Wrong (A): Allocation by profit-sharing ratios applies to nonrecourse liabilities, not recourse liabilities. Recourse debt follows economic risk of loss, which falls entirely on the guarantor.
Wrong (B): LLC members can receive basis increases from partnership-level liabilities under Sec. 752, regardless of their limited liability status as members.
Wrong (C): Equal allocation ignores the guarantee. Only Member A bears economic risk of loss, so the entire $100,000 is allocated to A, not split equally.$EXPL$
