-- Q2531: Business Structures [medium/L2]
-- Issues: #3
UPDATE questions SET
  explanation = $EXPL$Correct (D): Under IRC Sec. 164(f), taxpayers may deduct 50% of self-employment tax as an above-the-line adjustment to gross income (for AGI) on Form 1040. This deduction approximates the employer''s share of FICA that would be deductible by an employer.
Wrong (A): The SE tax deduction does not reduce Schedule C net income directly. It is a separate adjustment on Form 1040 that reduces AGI.
Wrong (B): Self-employment tax is partially deductible. IRC Sec. 164(f) specifically allows a deduction for half of the SE tax paid.
Wrong (C): The deduction is an above-the-line adjustment to gross income, not an itemized deduction on Schedule A. It is available regardless of whether the taxpayer itemizes.$EXPL$
